### UniApp API - manual tests
### How to use:
###   1) Start the server:  uvicorn api.main:app --reload
###   2) Install the "REST Client" extension in VS Code
###   3) Click "Send Request" above each request, top to bottom
### (Prefer curl/PowerShell? See the bottom of this file.)

@base = http://127.0.0.1:8000

### 1. Register - INVALID password (expect 400)
POST {{base}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Leila Tran", "email": "leila.tran@university.com", "password": "abc" }

### 2. Register - OK (expect 200). This one is @named so we can reuse the id.
# @name register
POST {{base}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Leila Tran", "email": "leila.tran@university.com", "password": "Aabcdef123" }

### reuse the new student id in the next requests
@sid = {{register.response.body.id}}

### 3. Register same email again (expect 409 already exists)
POST {{base}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Leila Tran", "email": "leila.tran@university.com", "password": "Aabcdef123" }

### 4. Login - OK (expect 200)
POST {{base}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Leila Tran", "email": "leila.tran@university.com", "password": "Aabcdef123" }

### 5. Login - wrong password (expect 401)
POST {{base}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "leila.tran@university.com", "password": "Wrongpass999" }

### 6. Get one student (expect 200)
GET {{base}}/students/{{sid}}

### 7. Enrol a subject (expect 200). Send this 4 times.
POST {{base}}/students/{{sid}}/subjects

### 8. Enrol the 5th time (expect 409 - only 4 allowed)
POST {{base}}/students/{{sid}}/subjects

### 9. List the student's subjects (expect 200, array of subjects)
GET {{base}}/students/{{sid}}/subjects

### 10. Remove a subject by its code - replace 007 with a real code from step 9 (expect 200)
DELETE {{base}}/students/{{sid}}/subjects/007

### 11. Change password - wrong current password (expect 401)
PUT {{base}}/students/{{sid}}/password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "current_password": "Wrongpass999", "new_password": "Newpass123" }

### 11b. Change password (expect 200)
PUT {{base}}/students/{{sid}}/password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "current_password": "Aabcdef123", "new_password": "Newpass123" }

### ---------- Admin ----------

### 12. List all students (expect 200)
GET {{base}}/admin/students

### 13. Group students by grade (expect 200)
GET {{base}}/admin/students/grouped

### 14. Partition PASS / FAIL (expect 200)
GET {{base}}/admin/students/partition

### 15. Remove a non-existent student (expect 404)
DELETE {{base}}/admin/students/000000

### 16. Remove our student (expect 200)
DELETE {{base}}/admin/students/{{sid}}

### 17. Clear all data (expect 200)
DELETE {{base}}/admin/students

### 18. Recent changes log (expect 200)
GET {{base}}/admin/log?limit=20

### =======================================================================
### Same tests with curl (run in a terminal while the server is running):
###
### curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/register -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d "{\"name\":\"Leila Tran\",\"email\":\"leila.tran@university.com\",\"password\":\"Aabcdef123\"}"
### curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/login    -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d "{\"name\":\"Leila Tran\",\"email\":\"leila.tran@university.com\",\"password\":\"Aabcdef123\"}"
### curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/students/<ID>/subjects
### curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/students/<ID>/subjects
### curl -X DELETE http://127.0.0.1:8000/students/<ID>/subjects/<CODE>
### curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/students
###
### PowerShell (Invoke-RestMethod):
###
### $b = @{ name="Leila Tran"; email="leila.tran@university.com"; password="Aabcdef123" } | ConvertTo-Json
### $s = Invoke-RestMethod -Method Post -Uri http://127.0.0.1:8000/register -ContentType application/json -Body $b
### Invoke-RestMethod -Method Post -Uri "http://127.0.0.1:8000/students/$($s.id)/subjects"
### Invoke-RestMethod -Uri http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/students
